body:
> IDK. This issue occurs in my project and in the Library Asset example with the same rhythmic delay jitter/stutter rate and the fix I use works equally well for both the example and my project.

The video of the Library Asset example you posted shows regular stutter (frames presented ABBC instead of ABCD). The video of your game that you posted shows the camera and airships (but not the particle FXs) **going backwards in time**.

> [vulkaninfo-3060ti-sytem.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19222891/vulkaninfo-3060ti-sytem.txt)
> [vulkaninfo-3070ti-system.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19222895/vulkaninfo-3070ti-system.txt)

Thanks!

Unfortunately you have nothing weird installed.

I do have a question though: What's the current value of `rendering/rendering_device/vsync/swapchain_image_count` for your project? Does the stutter change if you change that value? (valid values for your system should be `[2; 8]` but Godot will only let you set the value to `[2; 4]`).

**Edit:** And what about `rendering/rendering_device/vsync/frame_queue_size` ?

Interesting values to try:

- frame_queue_size = 2; swapchain_image_count = 2;
- frame_queue_size = 2; swapchain_image_count = 3;
- frame_queue_size = 3; swapchain_image_count = 3;
- frame_queue_size = 3; swapchain_image_count = 4;
- frame_queue_size = 3; swapchain_image_count = 2;

@darksylinc 

> Quick Check: Is that CSV you uploaded with the version using V-Sync with stutters, or the version with MaxFPS=60 and VSync off? Because judging at the data, it looks like the latter? 😵

Vsync with stutter. Not the smooth MaxFPS=60 No vsync.
